Kinnan doubles every nonland mana source you tap, which means the deck does not need to build a board — it needs to find two cards. Basalt Monolith taps for three, Kinnan makes it four, and untapping costs three: one mana of profit, repeated forever. The rest of the deck is redundancy for that line, a second and third combo that do the same job, and enough interaction to survive to turn five.

# The commander
Kinnan, Bonder Prodigy :: two mana, and every nonland permanent you tap for mana produces one extra. His {5}{G}{U} ability then digs five deep and puts a non-Human creature onto the battlefield — which is how unlimited mana becomes a board.
Delighted Halfling :: uncounterable mana for legendary spells. This is how Kinnan resolves against a table holding up blue mana.
Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu :: creature abilities work as though hasty, and he taps for two mana toward them — three with Kinnan.

# The three combos
Basalt Monolith :: with Kinnan, four mana in and three to untap. Unlimited colourless, from two cards.
Freed from the Real :: on Bloom Tender with green and blue among your permanents, Bloom Tender taps for {G}{U} and untapping costs {U}. That is a net green every cycle, and Kinnan makes it more.
Bloom Tender :: the other half, and a fine two-drop on its own.
Isochron Scepter :: imprint Dramatic Reversal. {2} and a tap untaps every nonland permanent, and with Kinnan doubling a handful of rocks the loop pays for itself.
Dramatic Reversal :: also just a very large ritual when you have a board and no Scepter.
Devoted Druid :: untaps itself twice for free, which is a burst rather than a loop — but it is a one-card ritual that Kinnan doubles, and it is a Green Sun's Zenith target for one mana.

# What the mana buys
Walking Ballista :: the kill. {4} per counter, remove counters to ping. With unlimited mana it shoots the whole table, and without it, it is flexible removal.
Thrasios, Triton Hero :: {4} to draw. Unlimited mana draws your entire library, and he is castable on turn two.
Kinnan, Bonder Prodigy :: the {5}{G}{U} ability activated repeatedly puts every relevant creature onto the battlefield without casting a single spell.
Finale of Devastation :: at X of ten, a tutor and a lethal pump at once.
Hullbreaker Horror :: uncounterable, flash, and with unlimited spells it bounces their entire board.

# Finding the pieces
Trophy Mage :: fetches a three-mana artifact, which is Basalt Monolith.
Drift of Phantasms :: transmute for three — Basalt Monolith again — and it blocks fliers while you wait.
Muddle the Mixture :: a counterspell, or transmute for two: Isochron Scepter, Bloom Tender or Agatha's Soul Cauldron.
Moonsilver Key :: fetches any artifact with a mana ability.
Fabricate :: any artifact, to hand.
Transmute Artifact :: trades a rock for the rock you need.
Green Sun's Zenith :: any green creature onto the battlefield — Bloom Tender for two, Devoted Druid for two.
Chord of Calling :: instant speed, convoke, any creature.
Nature's Rhythm :: the sorcery version, with harmonize to buy it back.
Formidable Speaker :: tutors a creature and untaps a permanent every turn.

# The mana base of permanents
Sol Ring :: turn one, doubled by Kinnan.
Mana Vault :: three on turn one, four with Kinnan.
Lotus Petal :: free.
Mox Opal :: metalcraft comes quickly.
Mox Amber :: live the moment Kinnan or Thrasios resolves.
Birds of Paradise :: fixing that Kinnan doubles.
Llanowar Elves :: two green from a one-drop.
Elvish Mystic :: the second copy.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the third.
Elvish Spirit Guide :: a free green from your hand.
Springleaf Drum :: taps a summoning-sick dork, doubled.
Gene Pollinator :: taps any permanent for mana, doubled.
Enduring Vitality :: every creature taps for any colour, and it returns as an enchantment when it dies.
Badgermole Cub :: an extra green per creature tapped for mana.
Simic Signet :: fixing.
Talisman of Curiosity :: the same.
Seedborn Muse :: untaps everything on all three opponents' turns, which with Kinnan is three extra pools per round.
Copy Artifact :: a second Basalt Monolith or a copy of their best rock.
Phyrexian Metamorph :: the same, and it copies creatures.

# Interaction
Force of Negation :: free on their turn.
Pact of Negation :: free now, and you win before the upkeep.
Mana Drain :: counter, and the mana goes toward the combo.
Flusterstorm :: nearly unbeatable in a counter war.
Swan Song :: one mana for a wrath or an enchantment.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: the same for anything noncreature.
Dispel :: one mana for the counterspell aimed at your combo.
Delay :: a hard answer for two mana that also buys three turns.
Misdirection :: free, and it turns their removal or tutor into yours.
Veil of Summer :: one mana that beats blue and black interaction and draws.
Force of Vigor :: free on their turn, and it destroys two artifacts or enchantments.
Nature's Claim :: one mana for any artifact or enchantment.
Pongify :: one mana, kills anything.
Chain of Vapor :: bounce anything, including your own permanent in response to removal.
Gilded Drake :: two mana to take their commander.
Spellskite :: redirects the removal aimed at Kinnan for two life.
Endurance :: free graveyard hate at instant speed on a 3/4 reach body.
Amphibian Downpour :: flash and storm; on a long turn it makes the table's commanders into 1/1 Frogs.

# Card flow
Rhystic Study :: their turns pay for yours.
Mystic Remora :: the strongest card in the deck on turns one through four.
Sylvan Library :: with this much selection, the four-life payments are nearly always right.
Faerie Mastermind :: flash, flies, draws off their extra draws.
Wan Shi Tong, Librarian :: scales, draws on entry, and grows off every tutor at the table.
Nezahal, Primal Tide :: uncounterable, draws on their noncreature spells, and protects itself from removal.
Agatha's Soul Cauldron :: exiles graveyards, and it hands the abilities of exiled creatures to anything with a +1/+1 counter — Walking Ballista in particular.
Borne Upon a Wind :: everything gains flash, so the whole combo can happen on their end step.
Colossal Skyturtle :: a big flier, or channel it for a bounce or a graveyard return without ever casting it.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep acceleration and a combo half. Sol Ring plus Kinnan is a keep; four lands and a Rhystic Study is not, because the deck's whole plan is two specific cards on turn four or five.
Protect the Kinnan cast. Delighted Halfling makes him uncounterable, and Force of Negation or Pact of Negation costs nothing to hold. Losing him mid-setup is usually losing the game.
Trophy Mage, Drift of Phantasms, Moonsilver Key and Transmute Artifact all point at Basalt Monolith. Treat them as four more copies of the combo rather than as value creatures.
With unlimited mana, activate Kinnan before you cast from hand. Putting creatures onto the battlefield from the library never uses the stack in a way a counterspell can answer.
